🧭 Understanding Event, Metric, and Dimensional Cardinality in New Relic (Using OpenTelemetry Kubernetes)

⸻

🧩 1. Event Data

🔹 Definition

Events in New Relic are discrete, timestamped occurrences that represent something that happened once — e.g., a pod restarted, a deployment scaled, or a request span completed.
They are stored as individual rows (immutable) in event tables like Span, Log, or K8sEvent.

Events are high-granularity and best for debugging, tracing, and auditing.

⸻

🔹 Example 1 – Kubernetes Pod Creation Event

Emitted via the OpenTelemetry k8sobjectsreceiver:

{
  "event.reason": "Created",
  "event.type": "Normal",
  "k8s.namespace.name": "checkout",
  "k8s.pod.name": "checkout-api-56f7d5b99c-2jzdp",
  "message": "Created container checkout-api",
  "timestamp": 1731888000
}

NRQL Query

FROM K8sEvent 
SELECT latest(message) 
WHERE event.reason = 'Created' 
  AND k8s.namespace.name = 'checkout'


⸻

🔹 Example 2 – Span Event for a Checkout Request

FROM Span 
SELECT average(duration) 
WHERE service.name = 'checkout-service' 
  AND k8s.namespace.name = 'prod' 
SINCE 30 minutes ago

→ Analyzes average latency per request span inside your Kubernetes service.

⸻

✅ Best For
	•	Tracing distributed requests
	•	Debugging pod-level failures
	•	Visualizing log or event timelines

⸻

📈 2. Metric Data

🔹 Definition

Metrics are aggregated numerical measurements collected at intervals — typically via the OpenTelemetry receivers such as
kubeletstatsreceiver, k8sclusterreceiver, or k8sobjectsreceiver.
They summarize data over time rather than capturing each occurrence.

Metrics appear in the Metric table (generic) or specialized sample tables like K8sContainerSample, K8sPodSample, SystemSample.

⸻

🔹 Example 1 – Container CPU Usage Metric

Collected by kubeletstatsreceiver:

FROM Metric 
SELECT average(k8s.container.cpu.usageCores) 
WHERE k8s.pod.name = 'checkout-api-56f7d5b99c-2jzdp' 
TIMESERIES 1 minute

Equivalent OpenTelemetry metric:

Name: k8s.container.cpu.usageCores
Type: Gauge
Attributes: {cluster="prod-cluster", namespace="checkout", container="checkout-api"}


⸻

🔹 Example 2 – Node Memory Utilization

FROM Metric 
SELECT average(k8s.node.memory.usagePercent) 
WHERE k8s.node.name LIKE 'ip-10-0-%' 
TIMESERIES


⸻

🔹 Example 3 – Pod Restart Count

FROM Metric 
SELECT max(k8s.pod.restart.count) 
WHERE k8s.namespace.name = 'checkout' 
FACET k8s.pod.name 
SINCE 1 hour ago


⸻

✅ Best For
	•	Dashboards & performance trends
	•	Alert conditions
	•	Cluster health and capacity planning

