⸻

🧰 6. Practical Pipeline Recommendations (OTel Collector)

receivers:
  - k8scluster
  - kubeletstats

processors:
  transform:
    metric_statements:
      - delete_key(attributes, "pod_uid")
      - delete_key(attributes, "container_id")
      - set(attributes["deployment"], attributes["k8s.deployment.name"])
  groupbyattrs:
    keys: ["cluster", "namespace", "deployment"]
  batch:
    timeout: 5s

exporters:
  - newrelic

service:
  pipelines:
    metrics:
      receivers: [k8scluster, kubeletstats]
      processors: [transform, groupbyattrs, batch]
      exporters: [newrelic]

→ This pipeline ensures low cardinality, high signal metrics flow into New Relic.

⸻

🧭 7. Summary Takeaways
	•	Use events for deep debugging (per-occurrence insights).
	•	Use metrics for system trends (aggregated views).
	•	Continuously optimize dimensional cardinality to control cost and query speed.
	•	Apply OTel processors like transform, groupbyattrs, batch before export.
	•	Monitor cardinality trends in New Relic UI.

